    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10">

                <pb facs="0113" n="19" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg19"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Ewing.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-04-01"><hi rendition="#italic">April 1,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 200.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information a copy of a
                    communication of the 30th ultimo, from the Secretary of Agriculture transmitting
                    a letter received by him from Messrs. Patterson, Ramsay &amp; Co., steamship
                    agents and brokers, Baltimore, concerning the alleged opening of the ports of
                    Belgium to cattle from the Netherlands, and to the recent discussion of the
                    subject in the Belgian Chamber of Representatives.</p>
                <p>A report of the debates in question will be found on pages 267 et seq. (session
                    of March 10, 1896) of the official journal of the proceedings of the Chamber of
                    Representatives. A copy thereof is not sent to you as you doubtless have ready
                    access at Brussels to the official reports of the debates.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to make full inquiries in regard to the matter complained of
                    and to ascertain whether the Belgian Government is willing to remove any
                    discrimination which may now be made against the importation of American cattle
                    in favor of those imported from the Netherlands or any other countries.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d10-a1.xml" xpointer="d10-a1"/>
